    "summary": "The private M0-A interview path is deployed through acknowledged-batch proposal admission, value-minimized review composition, partial acceptance for selected ordinary batch Candidates, individual terminal review for sensitive or explicitly single-review Candidates, a separate default-off iOS QA review consumer, a deployed value-minimized QA-only interview-session state read, a deployed QA-only natural-input session command contract, a lease-bound typed iOS natural-input QA client, and a double-gated Echo QA keyboard entry. The automatic Echo UIQA uses an in-memory fake client so it makes no backend request, private persistence write, voice turn, or Digital Human request; manual QA continues to use the deployed private command contract. Natural input receipts and ViewState never retain message text, and a valid submission clears the UI input immediately. The flow creates no Source, Candidate, DecisionReceipt, MemoryVersion, Projection, provider request, legacy Archive/KBLite write, or public Echo UI. A separate deployed M0-B sidecar may count coverage only from immutable Owner confirmation receipts bound to the exact current MemoryVersion content hash; inline annotations, KBLite facts and model labels never qualify. It does not change this active M0-A Work Item, create a public recommendation surface, or promote Registry status. The next boundary is a recorded M0-A public product-surface Gate; the existing full-screen Echo remains unmodified until that Gate is complete."
